    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\t\r\n\t\r\n\t\r\n\t\r\n\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"margin-bottom:0.2in\"><tt><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">Dear all, </span></font></font></font></tt><br>\r\n<tt><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">I have measured a tissue microarray which contains many tissue samples and each sample has regions with diseased and healthy tissue. </span></font></font></font></tt>\r\n<tt><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">This means I need to assign a sample name as well as a diagnosis to each pixel. </span></font></font></font></tt>\r\n<tt><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">The assignment of the diagnosis worked well as elsewhere proposed in this forum:<br><br></span></font></font></font></tt><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">normal </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">select</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">msidata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">150</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>diseased</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">select</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">msidata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">150</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>diagnosis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">character</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">msidata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>diagnosis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;normal&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>diagnosis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">diseased</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;diseased&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>diagnosis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">diagnosis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>msidata$diagnosis </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> diagnosis</span></div></code></div><br><tt><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">But I found no satisfying way to do the same for sample names<tt><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">, </font></tt></span></font></font></font></tt><tt><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">I tried </span></font></font></font></tt>\r\n<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">sample1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">select</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">msidata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">150</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sample2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">select</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">msidata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mz</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">150</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sample_names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">character</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ncol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">msidata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sample_names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;sample1&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sample_names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;sample2&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sample_names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">factor</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample_names</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>msidata$sample </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample_names</span></div></code></div><br>This looks ok on first glance, but does not work with PLS, PCA,...<br>\r\n<tt><font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">s</span></font></font></font></tt><tt><font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">ampleNames(msidata)</span></font></font></font></tt>\r\n<font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">[1] &quot;sample1&quot; &quot;sample2&quot;</font></font>\r\n\r\n<a name=\"m_-690583307212790984_rstudio_console_output4\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><tt><font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">validObject(msidata)</span></font></font></font></tt>\r\n<font color=\"#c5060b\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">Error in validObject(msidata) : </font></font></font>\r\n<font color=\"#c5060b\">  <font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">invalid class “MSImageSet” object: sample names differ between pixelData and protocolData</font></font></font>\r\n\r\n<a name=\"m_-690583307212790984_rstudio_console_output5\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><tt><font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">test = PLS(msidata,y=msidata$diagnosis, ncomp=2)</span></font></font></font></tt>\r\n<font color=\"#c5060b\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">PLS: Centering data.</font></font></font>\r\n<font color=\"#c5060b\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">PLS: Fitting partial least squares components.</font></font></font>\r\n<font color=\"#c5060b\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">Error in `sampleNames&lt;-`(`*tmp*`, value = c(&quot;sample1&quot;, &quot;sample2&quot;)) : </font></font></font>\r\n<font color=\"#c5060b\">  <font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">number of new names (2) should equal number of rows in AnnotatedDataFrame (1)</font></font></font>\r\n\r\nDoes anyone know how to correctly assign sample names within one MSI datafile? <br><br>Thanks in advance,<br>Melanie <br><tt><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt\" size=\"3\"><span style=\"font-weight:normal\"></span></font></font></font></tt></pre>\r\n\r\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "EHjn_2IEDQAJ",
   "from": "kbemis",
   "author": "6033d3c0e7d242fa",
   "date": "2018-05-15T17:29:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: Assigning sample names to pixels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The $sample column and sampleNames() method are special, and they actually correspond to the slide/run. You are saying these observations come from separate slides / separate runs. If that&#39;s what you intend to do, then it&#39;s a little convoluted, but you do something like this:<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><div>varMetadata(msidata)[&quot;sample&quot;,&quot;labelType&quot;] &lt;- &quot;dim&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>protocolData(msidata) &lt;- AnnotatedDataFrame(</div><div><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>data=data.frame(row.names=sampleNames(msidata)))</div><div><br></div><div>msidata &lt;- regeneratePositions(msidata)</div></div></code></div><br>If that&#39;s not what you mean to do, then choose a different name for the column besides &quot;sample&quot;, which is treated specially and particular expectations for it.</div><div><br></div><div>-Kylie</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pTBveYagAQAJ",
   "from": "Melanie Föll",
   "author": "db2a70d9b31cb1f7",
   "date": "2018-05-29T07:13:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: Assigning sample names to pixels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Kylie, <br></div><div><br></div><div>thanks a lot for your help, the sample assignment works now.<br></div><div><br></div><div>As I have a single slide (run) with many samples you are right, it is more convenient to define a new name such as msidata$sample_name and then also define a fold such as msidata$fold and then run the PLS with msidata$diagnosis and msidata$fold (instead of msidata$sample). <br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks again,</div><div>Melanie<br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "oaw-C1EkAgAJ",
   "from": "kbemis",
   "author": "6033d3c0e7d242fa",
   "date": "2018-05-30T21:16:14Z",
   "subject": "Re: Assigning sample names to pixels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, the &quot;$sample&quot; column naming can be misleading if you have multiple samples per slide. In retrospect, it should have been called &quot;$run&quot;, and there will probably be an version sometime in the future where that will be the case.<div><br></div><div>-Kylie</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
